       94  == Economy {{Citation needed|reason=Not in 2024 Census Data|date=February 2026}} ==
       95  [[File:Straseni TV Mast 8.jpg|thumb|Strășeni TV mast]]
       96  The main branches of the economy are [[agriculture]] and [[manufacturing]]. [[Soil]] and [[Climate|climatic]] conditions favor the growth of [[cereals]], [[sunflower]], [[grapes]], and other crops. The mineral resources in the district are stone, [[gravel]], pebbles and sand for building in [[Micăuț
       97  [[Arable land]] occupies 18,903 ha (25.9%) of the total land, [[vineyards]] occupy 8292 ha (11.3%), plantations of [[orchards]] 3386 ha (4.6%), 3244 ha of [[grassland]] (4.4%), 242 ha of fruit trees (0.3%), some 451 ha (0.6%).
       98  == Education ==
       99  In district there are 42 educational institutions, with a total of 10,721 students. Currently,{{When|date=September 2025}} there are 1040 teachers.{{Citation needed|reason=Not in 2024 Census Data|date=February 2026}}
      100  ==Politics==
      101  {{Update|date=February 2026}}
      102  In Strășeni district, support for right-wing politics was represented by the [[Alliance for European Integration]] (AEI). The [[Moldovan Communist Party]] (PCRM) had a continuous fall in the three elections from 2009 to 2010. During the elections AEI had an increase of 73.0%.
